== 2. a post binds only what the author annotated ==
ok   a clean post: name=Ada email=ada@example.com age=36 sub=on score=99.5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   a body naming a field the author did not annotate: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[is_admin] errors=[]
ok   a plus and a percent-twenty are both spaces: name=Ada B email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   a value is trimmed before it is measured: name=Al email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[name: name must be 3 to 12 characters]
ok   a missing required field: name= email= age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[name: name is required | email: email is required]
ok   a blank required field is missing too: name= email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[name: name is required]
ok   too long: name=Bartholomew Fitzwilliam email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[name: name must be 3 to 12 characters]
ok   a number that is not one: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
ok   a number outside its range: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=7 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be between 18 and 120]
ok   a float outside its range: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=100.5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be between 0 and 100]
ok   a float on the boundary is inside it: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=100 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   a checked box binds true: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=on score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   an unchecked box posts nothing and binds false: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   a checkbox value nobody's browser sends: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[subscribe: subscribe must be true or false]
-- the body parser
ok   an empty body has no fields: 0
ok   a key with no value: a=
ok   a repeated key keeps the last: a=2
ok   an empty pair is skipped: a=1
ok   a nameless pair is skipped: a=2
ok   a value carrying an equals sign: a=1=2
ok   a plus in a body is a space: a b
ok   an encoded plus stays a plus: a+b

== 3. the antiforgery token ==
a token at t=1000: 1900.ac52c8491de8cd2bde19c700e075d0c34ca1ce6e1e123ec0972514fb83335b2b
ok   the expiry is the head: 1900.
ok   the mac is sha256 in hex: 64
ok   the whole token, against Python's hmac: 1900.ac52c8491de8cd2bde19c700e075d0c34ca1ce6e1e123ec0972514fb83335b2b
ok   the token it issued: the token is valid
ok   one second before it expires: the token is valid
ok   the same token in another session: the antiforgery token does not match this session and form
ok   the same token on another form: the antiforgery token does not match this session and form
ok   the same mac under another expiry: the antiforgery token does not match this session and form
ok   one byte of the mac changed: the antiforgery token does not match this session and form
ok   the moment it expires: the antiforgery token has expired
ok   long after it expires: the antiforgery token has expired
ok   no token at all: the form carried no antiforgery token
ok   a token with no session: the request carried no session, so no token could belong to it
ok   a token with no separator: the antiforgery token is malformed
ok   a token whose expiry is not a number: the antiforgery token is malformed
ok   a token with an empty mac: the antiforgery token is malformed
ok   a forged token carrying an expiry in the past: the antiforgery token does not match this session and form
ok   a five-second lifetime expires in five seconds: 1005.
ok   and it is valid until then: the token is valid
ok   and not one tick past: the antiforgery token has expired
ok   two triples that would collide without length prefixes do not
-- the safe methods
ok   GET is safe
ok   HEAD is safe
ok   OPTIONS is safe
ok   POST is not
ok   DELETE is not
ok   a method nobody has heard of is not

