== 7. a failed post comes back as it was typed ==
ok   a value that did not parse: posted=true name=[Ada] email=[a@b.c] age=[twelve] model.age=41
ok   a value that parsed and broke a rule: posted=true name=[Ada] email=[a@b.c] age=[7] model.age=7
ok   a value that parsed to something spelled differently: posted=true name=[Ada] email=[a@b.c] age=[007] model.age=7
ok   a value is shown as it was judged, not as it arrived: posted=true name=[Al] email=[a@b.c] age=[36] model.age=36
ok   a box the user emptied stays empty: posted=true name=[] email=[a@b.c] age=[36] model.age=36
ok   a field the body did not carry falls back to the model: posted=true name=[SEED] email=[seed@example.com] age=[41] model.age=41
ok   a state no post produced says so
ok   and every box falls back: 41
ok   including one whose fallback is empty: 
ok   the posted map holds the @fields the body carried, and only those: age,email,name
ok   and the values are the trimmed text: twelve
ok   an unannotated name is ignored, not echoed: is_admin
ok   the result knows a post produced it

== 8. a whole number and a decimal, as a person spells them ==
-- leading zeros and signs
ok   a leading zero is not a syntax error: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   all zeros is zero, and then the range has its say: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be between 18 and 120]
ok   a plus sign: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   a minus sign binds and then breaks the range: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=-5 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be between 18 and 120]
-- and what is still refused
ok   a number too large for an int: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
ok   the same number written with leading zeros is still too large: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
ok   digits with something after them: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
ok   a sign and nothing else: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
ok   a decimal is not a whole number: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=0 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[age: age must be a whole number]
-- a route still has the stricter rule
ok   a route accepts the canonical spelling
ok   and refuses one with a leading zero
ok   a form accepts both
ok   with the same value: 7
ok   and neither accepts an overflow
-- decimals
ok   a fraction: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=7.5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   no digits before the point: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0.5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   no digits after it: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
ok   an exponent, which is what a number input sends for a big value: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=100 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[]
-- the three values to_float reads and no form should
ok   nan is not a number a form takes: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   nor is infinity: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   nor a hexadecimal spelling of a different value: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   and an exponent that overflows to infinity is refused with them: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   an exponent marker with no exponent: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   a point on its own: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=0 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be a number]
ok   a real number outside the range is still refused by the range: name=Ada email=a@b.c age=36 sub=off score=100.5 admin=no ignored=[] errors=[score: score must be between 0 and 100]

158 checks, 0 bad
